The unit's kernel (Intel's IOTG 4.14) has no DRM_IOCTL_I915_QUERY: its i915
ioctl 0x39 is GEM_GVTBUFFER, another call with another struct, so Mesa's
QUERY would reach it (tools/vk-trial/test/kernel414.c names it a HAZARD).
Mesa 22.x / 23.x ask it for the topology, the engines and the memory
regions, and fall back to GETPARAM and the defaults when it fails: fail it
here, before the kernel, as a kernel without QUERY answers (EINVAL).
Possibly what hung the car under Mesa 22.3's ANV (0.1.1): unproven.

--- a/src/intel/common/intel_gem.h
+++ b/src/intel/common/intel_gem.h
@@ -91,6 +91,10 @@ static inline int
 intel_i915_query_flags(int fd, uint64_t query_id, uint32_t flags,
                        void *buffer, int32_t *buffer_len)
 {
+   /* vizualyse: no I915_QUERY on the unit's 4.14 (0x39 is GEM_GVTBUFFER there) */
+   if (1)
+      return -EINVAL;
+
    struct drm_i915_query_item item = {
       .query_id = query_id,
       .length = *buffer_len,
